WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.757
Build a small evaluation set from the intended workload.

00:00:04.757 --> 00:00:12.685
Include common prompts, difficult edge cases, required formats, representative context lengths, and tasks with verifiable outcomes.

00:00:12.685 --> 00:00:20.612
Keep the base model, runtime, prompt template, sampling settings, and hardware constant while comparing quantization variants.

00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:25.822
Otherwise, the test cannot isolate precision as the changed variable.

00:00:25.822 --> 00:00:34.203
Compare at least one compact candidate, one practical middle candidate, and a higher-precision reference when hardware allows.

00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:46.208
Measure file size, loaded VRAM or RAM, model load time, time to first token, prompt-processing speed, generation speed, power or temperature if relevant, and errors.

00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:53.230
Run multiple trials so warm caches and random output do not determine the result.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.174
Score quality against predefined criteria.

00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:58.666
For coding, run tests.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.158
For extraction, compare fields.

00:01:01.158 --> 00:01:04.555
For structured output, validate the format.

00:01:04.555 --> 00:01:07.953
For analysis, review correctness and consistency.

00:01:07.953 --> 00:01:13.616
Long-context evaluation should use material that requires retrieval from different positions.

00:01:13.616 --> 00:01:21.996
Record failures, not only average impressions, because one serious instruction-following defect may outweigh a small speed gain.

00:01:21.996 --> 00:01:30.830
Keep a concise decision log with model revision, quantization file, runtime version, settings, hardware, measurements, and acceptance result.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:37.399
Select the lowest-resource option that meets quality and reliability requirements with memory headroom.

00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:43.062
Revisit the decision when the model, runtime, hardware, or workload changes.

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:48.725
Testing turns quantization from a label into an evidence-based deployment choice.
